WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.720
It was certainly understandable why so&nbsp;
many Dexter fans were skeptical of Dexter:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.080
New Blood when Showtime first&nbsp;
announced plans for the series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.480
The last episode of "Dexter" is one of the&nbsp;
most universally despised series finales&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.880
in the history of television. However,&nbsp;
over the course of its first season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.600
Dexter: New Blood would seem to have proven&nbsp;
itself a valued continuation of the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.040
series. The penultimate episode of the reboot's&nbsp;
first season, Episode 9 "The Family Business",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:33.840
currently sits at a 9.7 out of 10 rating on&nbsp;
IMDb, certainly a far cry from the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.840
series finale of Dexter, which is currently&nbsp;
only managing 4.6 stars on the same site.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.080
As reviews and reactions for the finale&nbsp;
of Dexter: New Blood continue to flood in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.640
it will be interesting to see if fans of the&nbsp;
series prefer this as a more definitive ending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.320
or want to see it as the first part&nbsp;
of a new entry of the franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.600
Here's a quick explainer about where&nbsp;
the last episode leaves things.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.680
Originally introduced as the kind-hearted&nbsp;
owner of a local business, Kurt Caldwell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.480
played by Clancy Brown, is slowly revealed&nbsp;
to be a monster who murders helpless women.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.880
Even though Michael C. Hall’s Dexter Morgan&nbsp;
kills and dismembers Kurt in Episode 9,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.600
the late serial killer's presence still looms&nbsp;
large over the events of the season finale.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.400
Before he winds up sealed in plastic, Kurt&nbsp;
sets fire to Dexter's cabin and mails Iron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.960
Lake Police Chief Angela Bishop a letter&nbsp;
that proves Dexter killed Matt Caldwell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.680
Kurt's final actions are very reminiscent of&nbsp;
those of Arthur Mitchell (aka Trinity) played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:33.040
by John Lithgow in the Season 4 finale of the&nbsp;
original Dexter series. In that episode, Dexter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:38.320
murders Trinity and returns home only to discover&nbsp;
that Trinity has already murdered his wife, Rita,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:43.680
and left his son, Harrison, crying in a pool of&nbsp;
blood. Despite technically winning the battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.520
few would contest that Dexter&nbsp;
ultimately lost the war with Trinity.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.400
Similarly, Kurt's letter to Angela and his&nbsp;
subsequent burning of Dexter's cabin directly lead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.360
to Dexter's arrest in the finale. As she stands&nbsp;
over the smoldering remnants of Dexter's cabin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.640
Angela locates a titanium screw that previously&nbsp;
held Matt's leg together. With all the proof&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.240
she needs, Angela arrests Dexter for murder and&nbsp;
makes a quick call to one Angel Batista of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.120
Miami Metro Police Department. Once again,&nbsp;
Dexter's enemy bests him from the beyond.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.800
After decades of murder and dismemberment, Dexter&nbsp;
finally meets his own end in the last moments of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.680
Dexter: New Blood. The final episode sees the&nbsp;
famous serial killer cornered at all angles by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.400
his former girlfriend, who promises to extradite&nbsp;
the infamous Bay Harbor Butcher to Florida,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.720
where he will surely face the death penalty.&nbsp;
Unwilling to accept his fate, Dexter makes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:38.160
mad-dash escape from the jail, leaving a bloody&nbsp;
trail in the process. Dexter rushes to Harrison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.000
but the elder Morgan's killing of Sergeant&nbsp;
Logan is a step too far for the young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.800
serial killer in training, who recognizes&nbsp;
that Dexter's actions violate the code.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.880
At his son's urging, Dexter considers the&nbsp;
plethora of innocent people who have died as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:58.480
a result of his actions. We see flashes of Logan,&nbsp;
LaGüerta, Doakes, Lundy, Harry, Rita, and Debra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.520
all people who suffered untimely deaths because of&nbsp;
their proximity to Dexter. Faced with the truth of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:08.800
his past, Dexter admits that Harrison is right and&nbsp;
invites his son to shoot him in the chest. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:13.280
not exactly the same as showrunner Clyde Phillips'&nbsp;
original plan for the Dexter series finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.920
the highlighting of Dexter's truly innocent&nbsp;
victims represents a similar narrative choice in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:23.200
that he is finally forced to take responsibility&nbsp;
for his actions, just prior to his own death.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.920
Throughout Dexter and Dexter: New Blood, Dexter&nbsp;
makes it clear that he is unable to feel genuine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:33.520
emotion, despite how normal he may seem to&nbsp;
some people. In Season 1, Episode 1, he says,

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.240
"People fake a lot of human interactions,&nbsp;
but I feel like I fake them all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:41.120
and I fake them very well."
By the end of the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.480
Dexter admits that his emotional mimicry and&nbsp;
violent urges will always hurt those close to him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.240
He abandons Harrison to spare him the&nbsp;
suffering. In furtherance of this goal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.280
Dexter also initially refuses to have anything&nbsp;
to do with Harrison when he arrives in Iron Lake.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.320
However, despite pleas from Debra's postmortem&nbsp;
manifestation, Dexter eventually embraces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.120
Harrison as a son, teaching him the code&nbsp;
and even inviting him into his kill room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.440
Sadly, Debra's pleas would seem to have been&nbsp;
well founded. The code is ultimately proven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:13.920
unable to prevent Dexter from harming numerous&nbsp;
innocent people. Realizing that Dexter is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.560
person responsible for most of the suffering in&nbsp;
his life, Harrison openly blames his father for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:23.200
his mother's murder, his aunt's death, and&nbsp;
his own dark tendencies. Harrison screams,

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.640
"Open your eyes and look at what you've done!"

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.800
Slowly, Dexter comes to grips with the truth&nbsp;
in Harrison's words, telling his son that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:36.000
deserves a better life and a better father. Just&nbsp;
before Harrison shoots his father, Dexter notes,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:46.080
"I've never really felt&nbsp;
love. Real love. Until now."

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:50.080
It has certainly taken some time for&nbsp;
him to learn, but Dexter's final moments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:54.080
seem to offer him some understanding&nbsp;
of what it means to actually be human.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:58.080
It's difficult to tell where things could&nbsp;
go after this type of a finale. With the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.280
titular character dead, the future seems somewhat&nbsp;
limited. Of course, any speculation about any more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:08.240
potential seasons of Dexter: New Blood is bound&nbsp;
to focus on Harrison, who leaves Iron Lake with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:13.040
no specific destination in mind. As he departs&nbsp;
Iron Lake, Harrison reads an old letter written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.080
by Dexter to Hannah McKay, in which his father&nbsp;
affectionately refers to Harrison as his, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.840
"phantom limb" and says that a normal&nbsp;
life will never be possible for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.640
so long as he is around. While one interpretation&nbsp;
of this scene is that Harrison can live a normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:31.520
life now that his father is dead, a darker&nbsp;
interpretation is also equally likely.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:36.560
Harrison has previously displayed a multitude&nbsp;
of dark tendencies, much like his father. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.280
unclear if Harrison will be able to hold his Dark&nbsp;
Passenger at bay without his father's assistance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.520
However normal Harrison manages to make his&nbsp;
future, that voice which guides him could,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:49.760
at some point, take on the form of a&nbsp;
familiar face. In the original series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:54.640
Dexter's Dark Passenger is represented by&nbsp;
his deceased father and mentor, Harry Morgan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:59.040
Given Dexter's role in his son's life, it's&nbsp;
possible that Harrison's memory of his father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.280
could one day occupy the same function.&nbsp;
That voice in the finale might just be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:07.760
the beginning of Dexter's own postmortem&nbsp;
manifestation inside Harrison's head.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:11.200
While a show called "Harrison" probably&nbsp;
wouldn't have quite the same appeal as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.720
"Dexter," perhaps someone out there&nbsp;
is already trademarking something like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.520
"Dexter: Afterlife" with this very plan in mind.

